{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792315493,"nonce":"rZ47HgLeRQYoMWLDI3mS0lnOit8=","title":"mandelbrot checksum differs from hxcpp: fused multiply-add changes Haxe float results","message":"NUC, compiler/benchmarks/haxe/BMMandelbrotCode.hx at 7bd07974:\n- hxcpp (haxe 4.3.6 -cpp): `Checksum: 112790102`\n- `rayzor run --release` (Cranelift and tiered) and `rayzor run` (debug): `112798288`\n- `RAYZOR_NO_FMA=1 rayzor run --release`: `112790102`, matching hxcpp.\n\nHaxe Float is IEEE double with each operation rounded; contracting `a*b+c` into one fused operation changes the escape iteration of boundary points, so the program prints a different answer. The published mandelbrot time is measured on the fused (wrong) code. FMA formation needs to be off for Haxe code by default (or only where the result is provably identical), on every backend; re-measure mandelbrot/nbody/spectralnorm after.","files":null}]}